		<item>
			<title>StackSync website &amp; source code</title>
			<link>http://127.0.0.1/cloudspaces/news/89-stacksync-website-source-code</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="true">http://127.0.0.1/cloudspaces/news/89-stacksync-website-source-code</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<div class="feed-description"><p>Recently, we have published the <strong>community website</strong> of StackSync (<a href="http://stacksync.org" target="_blank">http://stacksync.org</a>) where we plan to keep users informed about the progress we are making. You can find documentation about how it is built, how to deploy it, or download links to get StackSync for a variaty of platforms.</p>
<p>We have also uploaded the <strong>source code to GitHub</strong> (<a href="http://github.com/stacksync" target="_blank">http://github.com/stacksync</a>) and, from this moment on, we will continue our development on GitHub. Feel free to contribute on any of the projects we are undertaking.</p></div>]]></description>
			<author>adrifx@gmail.com (Adrian Moreno)</author>
			<category>Blog entry</category>
			<pubDate>Tue, 03 Dec 2013 14:12:00 +0000</pubDate>
